   158	`C` is injective-linear in 192 coordinates disjoint from `h, D`, and `a`
   159	enters `F` linearly. Hence, with `F_0 := h^3 + (3/2)Dh`,
   160	
   161	```text
   162	J(F,G) = J(F_0, G) + (a/2)·J(h, G) + J(C, G) = J(F_0,G) + (a/2) D_G(h) + D_G(C),
   163	```
