   172	   image of `D_G` on the 193-dimensional subspace `V_C ⊕ k·h`": the
   173	   bounded-degree version of the mate/cokernel problem whose global form is
   174	   avenue 29's Gauss–Manin class. Residue functionals at places at infinity
   175	   of the fibres `G = T` (avenue 33; the R050 construction with `G` in the
   176	   role of `f`) are explicit left-null vectors of `D_G`, i.e. explicit
   177	   equations on the 246 nonlinear coordinates alone. This is exactly why
