@@ -0,0 +1,76 @@
+# Adversarial cross report — Sol 5.6 — ideation-20260906T1030Z
+
+Status: **JC2 UNRESOLVED; REDESIGN.** No proof, counterexample, properness result, source-family exclusion, or all-degree mechanism is obtained.
+
+## Custody and cutoff
+
+The current charged manifest has 14 unique rows and exactly 14 staged regular files. All 14 SHA-256 values match; the five collected submissions match `collection.json`, and every declared body byte/hash seal replays with one standalone terminator. I read the complete cross packet and every charged report. I did not read any live CROSS submission or uncharged live report/log and made no AWS, heavy-CAS, `jc2-lean`, shared-ledger, adapter, or external action.
+
+Blind collection closed at 11:19:59Z (`box/ideation-20260906T1030Z/collection.json:2-6`). The comparisons below judge only what each sealed submission proved by then. Later facts are separated and cannot repair a blind proof. No new exit-price assertion is made, so no `charge_basis` declaration applies.
+
+## Blind comparison: claims, not votes
+
+The strongest surviving proposal is one merged mechanism, independently approached rather than multiply voted: **global constant-rational elimination of most of the physical family’s 192-dimensional C block, with every compatibility row and `Zj*J0-1` retained**. Astra gives the most complete blind derivation, quotient discipline, and nilpotent/fill-in controls (`xmodel/ideation-20260906T1030Z-astra.md:87-141`); Sol states the appropriately provisional filtered-symbol/extraction contract (`xmodel/ideation-20260906T1030Z-sol56.md:155-264`); the coordinator correctly labels runtime benefit unknown (`xmodel/ideation-20260906T1030Z-coordinator.md:72-115`). This is a representation theorem, not an obstruction or a solver win. **NO_NEW_MECHANISM** survives for unrestricted JC2.
+
+The strongest blind overstatement is Opus’s jump from two generic rank-191 samples plus a uniform floor 188 to “rigid up to a constant everywhere” and effective dimension at most 248 (`xmodel/ideation-20260906T1030Z-opus5.md:9-20,163-187`). Its matrix uses positive rows, so its kernel condition is `J(C,G)` constant, not zero; generic modular rank cannot globalize. “Rank-drop exactly decomposable” also lacks the converse that the primitive generator lies in the actual C-space. Its inclusion of projected T2/T3 points in the physical locus does not prove strict containment or computational dominance (`ibid.:222-257`).
+
+Fable’s related argument treats the positive-only `(C,a)` block as though a kernel vector were C alone, omitting `P=C+(a/2)h`, and likewise lacks primitive-generator membership (`xmodel/ideation-20260906T1030Z-fable5.md:154-203`). Its numerical proposal is instrumentation, not infeasibility evidence: seconds-per-iteration and convergence are unmeasured, while `J0=1` and six gauge slices depend on an unproved grading/action (`ibid.:216-237,267-306,390-395`). The source-atlas/necessity cards name a real obligation but supply no actual new transformation; they are a test protocol, not a bridge. Novelty labels do not improve any of these proofs.
+
+One useful composition is: instantiate the constant-pivot C reduction as a circuit; use variable projection only inside that circuit to nominate nonlinear-base candidates or binding rows; retain the inverse row and all residuals; accept a hit only by exact reconstruction and evaluation in a stated nonzero finite Q-algebra. For proof-side use, prepend an explicit source-to-chart map with every localization complement. Numerical residuals and sampled inconsistency remain non-results.
+
+## Bottlenecks reranked
+
+Proof side:
+
+1. An all-degree, branch-complete source/receiver theorem plus a structural obstruction. The `24,063 -> 90 -> 64` census is only an `n<=200` regression population.
+2. At fixed `(99,66)`, source-to-gauged-stage-8 necessity. Until its actual group maps, supports, and complements are proved, a unit excludes only the tested family.
+3. A uniform receiver obstruction. K16’s all-`m`, both-factor, separate `b=0` product target is a useful prototype, not coverage of JC2.
+4. Individual chart decision cost.
+
+Counterexample side:
+
+1. Produce one exact characteristic-zero point of the complete physical-J family; source necessity is irrelevant in this direction.
+2. Search the thin nonlinear consistency locus after C reduction. Random exact base sampling will almost surely miss a proper closed locus and its failures say nothing.
+3. Obtain a decision/certificate economically. Verification after a candidate is already the comparatively cheap part.
+
+## Common post-cutoff facts — prospective use only
+
+- The producer-checked filtered theorem constructs 189 constant pivots and leaves degrees 22, 11, and 0, but the two nonconstant residual columns cannot be dropped (`xmodel/linear-c-filtered-pilot-astra-20260906.md:55-96,144-186`). Direct expansion is a negative cost result: after only 24 pivots, 668 positive rows already had 9,967,234 terms at the 300-second wall, versus 11,299,180 terms for the complete original build in 137.145 seconds (`xmodel/linear-c-structured-pilot-astra-20260906.md:70-128`). This refutes a construction win for that implementation, not circuit elimination generally.
+- Complete exact-Q `slimgb` timed out at 600.959 seconds/33.29 GiB; modular msolve crashed before F4 evidence. Neither decided the ideal. The unsigned-32-bit allocation overflow is proved, but its responsibility for SIGSEGV remains inference (`xmodel/full-j-solver-pilot-astra-20260906.md:84-127`).
+- The K16 gate confirms rational-to-polynomial return and an exact norm/differential reformulation, not polynomial nonexistence; the product target remains OPEN (`xmodel/k16-boundary-product-gate-fable5-20260906.md:15-61,71-75`). The new degree estimate merely reproduces the existing 145/227 endpoint (`xmodel/degree-estimate-interface-astra-20260906.md:24-48`).
+
+## Hostile audit of the transverse result
+
+Conditional on the reported literal source facts and the quoted common-generator theorem, the **full-coefficient** rank-191 proof is coherent. `G(X,0)` is monic quadratic; `J(P,G)=0` gives `G=phi(R), P=psi(R)`; restriction forces `deg(phi)` to be 1 or 2. The first case violates `deg P<=35`; the second forces a forbidden `W^33` term in P (`xmodel/linear-c-transverse-rank-astra-20260906.md:30-103`). This critically uses the exact W-line support, fixed top, characteristic zero, and absence of `W^33` from C. The supplied source/certificate artifacts are not charged here, so a dedicated different-model source/code gate remains mandatory.
+
+The nonreduced extension is limited but legitimate: rank 191 at every geometric fiber makes the maximal-minor ideal unit in the polynomial base ring, hence yields an abstract polynomial left inverse after arbitrary base change (`ibid.:148-165`). It does **not** exhibit one constant 191-minor, sparse Bezout coefficients, or affordable substitution (`ibid.:167-172`).
+
+Positive-only is different: deleting the constant output permits `J(P,G)=kappa`; `J(X,X^2+W)=1` is the explicit control. Positive-only `(C,a)` injectivity is proved only after assuming an actual Keller pair and cannot help prove its existence; it fails unconditionally at `D=b=0` (`ibid.:105-146`). Thus the post-cutoff theorem does not retroactively validate Opus or Fable.
+
+The 190-pivot lemma’s triangular calculation is sound on `V0={P:P(X,0)=0}`: the selected coefficient has diagonal `-2r` in a W-adapted basis (`ibid.:174-203`). But no actual 190-column source transform/minor or cost was emitted; one nonconstant C direction remains, and full rank supplies only a potentially expensive residual Bezout combination (`ibid.:204-212`). It is producer-checked, not promoted.
+
+## Cheapest discriminator
+
+Independently emit and replay that actual W-adapted 190-column basis and positive-row minor, then serialize **all** remaining rows and the inverse row as a circuit without expanding them. Assumptions: the frozen source hash/support, Q coefficients, unchanged 1,629-row target, and a passed source-interface gate.
+
+Use three deterministic exact controls: a small rational source assignment with its directly computed full-J coefficient vector as known output; the zero-J source, which must pass positive rows but fail the inverse row by `-1`; and one mutated pivot/row label, which must fail. Record completeness, row maps, DAG nodes, exact evaluation wall, and peak RSS against the same three assignments on the original stream. Existing measurements are 137.145 seconds/1.71 GiB for the original build and a failed 300-second/2.05 GiB partial expansion; the proposed 600-second/8-GiB cap and any speedup are estimates.
+
+Mismatch rejects the reduction instance. Cap, omitted row, or no threefold exact-evaluation improvement retains the theorem but stops performance work. A complete map with at least a threefold improvement licenses one paired solver benchmark, not a mathematical claim. Full-C rank itself cannot change if the theorem’s hypotheses hold; only failed support/line hypotheses or the positive-only/enlarged `(C,a)` map can change the relevant rank. No 1,000-start numerical run is licensed before exact-known-output, inverse-escape, and 53/128/256-bit agreement controls pass.
+
+## Systems and direction calls
+
+Choose only the read-only **audit-heading index**: two observed heading grammars can silently omit eight newest states (`xmodel/ideation-20260906T1030Z-fable5.md:239-256`). A 15-minute fail-closed fixture test has small opportunity cost and broader benefit than a report-format checker; its risk is false confidence after future grammar drift. Do not also fund catch-up or contract-checker work.
+
+| Direction | Call |
+|---|---|
+| Existing `.63` / `.73` jobs | **CONTINUE only to existing caps;** harvest exactly; timeout/nonunit has no force. |
+| Physical-J | **REDESIGN** around gated circuit C-reduction and calibrated candidate generation. No raw retry. |
+| Modular full-J | **STOP** until allocation-safe parsing is reviewed; then at most one capped telemetry run, with no Q inference. |
+| Direct T2/T3 / protected partials | **STOP scale-up, retain custody;** resume only after a source map and comparative cost case. |
+| K16 | **CONTINUE** the bounded all-`m` product obstruction; do not launch a separate norm-model solve. |
+| Source necessity | **CONTINUE** one explicit fixed-client map/complement audit; **stop** generic atlas prose without a map. |
+| Numerical projection | **REDESIGN** behind the stated controls and a fixed budget. |
+| R005, R050, generic Ni/rank, generic degree estimates | **STOP** automatic continuation. |
+| External sweep | Honor the existing clock; no duplicate sweep now. |
+
+<!-- BODY-END -->

