+The strongest surviving proposal is one merged mechanism, independently approached rather than multiply voted: **global constant-rational elimination of most of the physical family’s 192-dimensional C block, with every compatibility row and `Zj*J0-1` retained**. Astra gives the most complete blind derivation, quotient discipline, and nilpotent/fill-in controls (`xmodel/ideation-20260906T1030Z-astra.md:87-141`); Sol states the appropriately provisional filtered-symbol/extraction contract (`xmodel/ideation-20260906T1030Z-sol56.md:155-264`); the coordinator correctly labels runtime benefit unknown (`xmodel/ideation-20260906T1030Z-coordinator.md:72-115`). This is a representation theorem, not an obstruction or a solver win. **NO_NEW_MECHANISM** survives for unrestricted JC2.
+
+The strongest blind overstatement is Opus’s jump from two generic rank-191 samples plus a uniform floor 188 to “rigid up to a constant everywhere” and effective dimension at most 248 (`xmodel/ideation-20260906T1030Z-opus5.md:9-20,163-187`). Its matrix uses positive rows, so its kernel condition is `J(C,G)` constant, not zero; generic modular rank cannot globalize. “Rank-drop exactly decomposable” also lacks the converse that the primitive generator lies in the actual C-space. Its inclusion of projected T2/T3 points in the physical locus does not prove strict containment or computational dominance (`ibid.:222-257`).
