+One useful composition is: instantiate the constant-pivot C reduction as a circuit; use variable projection only inside that circuit to nominate nonlinear-base candidates or binding rows; retain the inverse row and all residuals; accept a hit only by exact reconstruction and evaluation in a stated nonzero finite Q-algebra. For proof-side use, prepend an explicit source-to-chart map with every localization complement. Numerical residuals and sampled inconsistency remain non-results.
